{
  "id": "medial-prefrontal-cortex",
  "term": "medial prefrontal cortex",
  "definition": "The medial prefrontal cortex is a brain region involved in goal-directed behavior, weighing value and reward, and aspects of social planning and self-insight. In humans, it is also linked to self-worth, and changes in its activity can influence how a person is perceived by others without that person being aware of the change.",
